<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 71,191 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 71,191 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 71,191 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 51,357 tonnes on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			24,262	    23,433</p>
<p>    Import cargo			46,929	    27,924</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port: Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    73,000	 Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-1	   18/2</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		17/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		72,944	 Johar		 18/2</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Warbah		 due</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    6,000	 Cielo-de-Selarno  19/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 2,293	 Ncc Jouf	    21/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
